      "side": 1,
      "message": "If CONFIG_USBC_VCONN isn\u0027t defined, then there is no way for the flag to be set.\n\nI think this is easier to read having a single condition than having two conditions where one doesn\u0027t have any logical value (i.e. TC_CHK_FLAG(port, TC_FLAGS_VCONN_ON) can never be true if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_USBC_VCONN) is false)\n\nI don\u0027t thinks this really costs us much code size and CONFIG_USBC_VCONN still controls whether we are using vconn or not (which I would image every users of the new stack will do).\n\n----\n\nI did confirm that there are no compiler errors when CONFIG_USBC_VCONN is defined or undefined.",
